These scripts effectively 'short-circuit' pbt by having the input and output basis sets formats specified.
For example, molext2molext expects Molpro external format for the input, and will write the same format.

For the scripts to run, the top-level pbt directory needs to be in your PYTHONPATH, which can be set using something like (in bash):
export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:$HOME/pbt

You may also want to add the pbt/scripts directory to your shell PATH.
